---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import AboutHead from "../components/AboutHead.astro";
---

<Layout title="about — fosskar" description="about fosskar">
  <AboutHead lang="en" />
  <p>
    i’m simon. i work as a devops engineer and sre on kubernetes and gitops,
    and outside of work i’m deep into open source: nix and nixos,
    self-hosting, and running and benchmarking (local) llms.
  </p>
  <p>
    there has always been a linux box running somewhere around me. for years it
    was a hobby: break something, read until it works again, move on to the
    next thing. in 2022 i went through a bootcamp to turn that into a job, and
    i’ve been working in devops since 2023.
  </p>
  <p>
    the hobby taught me to think in whole systems rather than single machines.
    the job taught me how much i dislike doing the same thing twice by hand,
    and that is what brought me to nixos: describe a machine once, rebuild it
    whenever.
  </p>
  <p>
    what usually gets me going is annoyance. when something bugs me long
    enough, i fix it properly instead of working around it, and i like that the
    result is mine. most of my side projects started that way; they’re on the
    <a href="/projects/">projects</a> page.
  </p>
  <p>
    i don’t try to understand everything. software is too big for that, and if
    you try, you stop making progress. i learn the parts i actually use, deep
    enough to fix them.
  </p>
  <p>
    i write things down when i want to remember them, when i want to show them
    to other people, or to document an experience or a process. that’s what
    the <a href="/wiki/">wiki</a> is for. the <a href="/blog/">blog</a> is for
    longer pieces.
  </p>
  <p>
    i’d like to work with nix professionally. if you’re hiring for that, have
    freelance work, or want to talk nix or kubernetes, write me on <a
      href="https://matrix.to/#/@fosskar:fosskar.de">matrix</a
    >. code is on <a href="https://github.com/fosskar">github</a>, mirrored to
    <a href="https://radicle.fosskar.eu">radicle</a>.
  </p>
</Layout>
